{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: Purified by (NH4)2SO4 precipitation and chromatographic methods. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (40%) to Cliotide T10. A: 20%, L: 17%, V=K: 11%. GRAVY: 0.87, mol Wt: 3995.89; mol formula: C193H315N46O44; mol ex coeff: 10020. Activity: active against E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 1 uM), S. aureus ATCC 25923 (MIC 4 uM), A. baumannii ATCC 19606 (MIC 2 ug/ml), and P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 (MIC 1 uM). MBC was 2-fold higher. Peptide stability: not heat stable at 90oC treatment for 1 h. Antimicrobial robustness: activity is lost at pH 2-5. pH-senstive to acidic conditions. activity is human serum-sensitive (25%). In vitro toxicity: human RBC: 18% lysis at 32 uM. HEK293 cells: 94% alive treated at 1-4 uM. Structure: predicted to be helical.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39886350", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Bioinform Biol Insights. 2025 Jan 29;19:11779322251315291. doi: 10.1177/11779322251315291. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05253", "source_id": "AP05253", "source_numeric_id": "05253", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05253", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Cliotide U1, a Novel Antimicrobial Peptide Isolated From Urtica Dioica Leaves", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
